# Reconstructed delta: work that was done in the working tree but never saved.
#
# This patch exists because the numbered stack stopped reproducing extern/decomp.
# Applying every patch to a clean checkout left 75 files different, and the
# difference was not a few stray edits -- whole fixes that README.md describes in
# detail lived only in the submodule working tree. The largest is the
# Event::m_data devirtualisation fix (the `->Payload()` / `std::launder`
# refactor); the rest is GameCube-layout and endian work (`NL_GC_LAYOUT` asserts,
# `u32` in place of `unsigned long` in overlaid structs, host-width pointer and
# record sizes) and the vertex-array/display-list work in `NL/glx`.
#
# Four numbered patches were folded in here rather than repaired, because none of
# them could apply at its own position in the stack any more:
#
#   093-host-skip-front-end-switch            -- authored against a tree that
#       already had patches/tmp applied, so its GameInfo.cpp context did not
#       exist yet when the decomp stage ran (see "Patch stage ordering" in
#       README.md). Its effect is included below and refined by patch 103.
#   095-size-shared-vertex-arrays-by-max-index -- the patch file itself was
#       corrupt: the hunk header claimed 6 context and 38 result lines for a body
#       carrying 5 and 36, and the leading `/**` context line was missing.
#   096-fix-zero-offset-packed-vertex-arrays   -- depended on glxLoadModel.cpp
#       content that was never in any patch.
#   097-size-shared-arrays-across-model        -- likewise, for
#       glxDisplayList.h/.cpp, glxLoadModel.cpp and glxSend.cpp.
#
# It is deliberately not split by theme. A file-level split was attempted and 57
# of the 75 files carry hunks from more than one theme, so any split would be an
# invented history rather than a recovered one. The narrative account of what
# these changes do, and why, is in README.md; this patch is what makes the tree
# reproducible again.
#
# Generated by diffing the working tree against a clean checkout with
# patches/decomp/*, patches/musyx/* and patches/tmp/* applied, so it applies as
# the first entry of the decomp-late stage.
#
#
